Id: sudo002i
Severity: INFO
Category: accounts
Check: check_sudo
References: sudoers(5)
Controls: CIS 5.4; NIST AC-6; ISO 8.2; CE User access control

Some sudo rules let their users run specific commands as root without
a password; the detail lists them, as "who: command". Packages add
such rules for helpers of their own (Linux Mint's driver and update
tools, for instance). Each is as safe as the command it names: one that
can be talked into running another program (an editor, a pager, a
shell script others can write) gives root to whoever may run it. This
is informational; worth a look when one is new.
